From 883de1732764ab7e9284c4c6b0c9ee403219f5bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:13:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] Meter: start and close with AION2

Settings' "Start and close with AION2" (on unless turned off) puts a small
watcher, a2tools-game-watch, in the desktop's autostart and starts it. Every
3 s it looks through /proc for the game, as the meter does; when the game
starts and no meter runs, it starts one with --with-game. Only such a meter
closes, 10 s after the game is gone (a quick restart of the game keeps it).
A meter started by hand behaves as always, also when started by hand while
one started with the game runs. A meter closed by hand while the game runs
is started again only at the game's next start. Turned off, the entry is
removed and the watcher stops by itself. It opens no window and sends
nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012bGvDj8ZmT41uucm2ufqo7
